WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.950
- People tell me that New York

00:00:04.077 --> 00:00:05.190
can be the best place in the world;

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.870
the most social place in the world.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.640
But it can also be the loneliest place

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.973
in the world as well.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.890
The goal of the supper club

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.593
is to bring people together.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.217
(orchestral music)

00:00:24.984 --> 00:00:27.470
My name is Vincent Woo,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:31.130
and I am known for running
a supper club called

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.590
Mr. Jones Supper Club.

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.170
Yeah, I'm gonna get the scallops.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.900
In the basement of my apartment.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:38.906
Chives.

00:00:38.906 --> 00:00:39.739
- [Man] Yeah.

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:43.700
- And a small basket of the shallots.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:48.350
It started when I got here
about three years ago.

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:52.540
I didn't know anyone and
I missed getting together

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.720
around the kitchen with
friends and eating.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.840
So I started with acquaintances,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.330
and then one thing led to another

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:01.153
and it sort of blew up.

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.300
I only do it two times a month.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:10.160
But the demand is over
two three years now.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.773
And that's rounding down.

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.120
Guests do not have to pay to come.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:20.180
You pay whatever you feel
like at the end of the night,

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.860
based on how much they
enjoyed the experience

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.543
and how much they can afford.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.210
I'm not formally trained in cooking.

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:33.353
Let's say YouTube is probably my teacher.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:37.483
Every month in Mr. Jones,
no menu is ever the same.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:42.450
Last Saturday we started
off with some burrata,

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.790
and then it was accompanied by tuna tartar

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.683
and topped with fried lotus root chips.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.760
Then we had scallop crudo.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.030
It also had a lot of
Asian flavors as well.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.050
Then we had the mushroom
on mushroom on mushroom,

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:00.740
which is like big chunky

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.443
maitake mushroom baked in the oven.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.200
I love doing this.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.050
I definitely have made friends from it.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.690
People have definitely made friends

00:02:14.690 --> 00:02:16.700
with each other from it as well.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.490
My first time like, you know,

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.509
finding long lost people together.

00:02:19.509 --> 00:02:20.342
- [Woman] Exactly.

00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:22.515
- [Vincent] I think it's
a good way just to stop

00:02:22.515 --> 00:02:25.270
and get people to be present sometimes

00:02:25.270 --> 00:02:28.300
with people without phones and just talk

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:29.500
and get to know someone.

00:02:30.975 --> 00:02:33.892
(orchestral music)

